   "title": "SHOT LOCK \u2014 style, camera and framing",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "A short clip from a 1933 newspaper comic strip, drawn in Fleischer-era rubber-hose cartoon style: confident smooth ink outlines of even weight, soft halftone dot shading, warm sepia duotone on aged grey-brown newsprint, every colour muted and desaturated as faded printing. The camera never moves and the framing never changes: one fixed head-and-shoulders frame with the same flat backdrop throughout, like a portrait slot that two characters take turns standing in. The clip begins on the character in the first frame and ends on the character in the last frame, and only ever those two characters appear."
   ],
   "color": "#223",
   "bgcolor": "#335"
  },
